  "observed_contract": [
    "NEGATIVE_INFERENCE_VARIANCE reports materially negative binned local-linear fitted variance in a primitive or polarized fit.",
    "INFERENCE_COVARIANCE_NOT_PSD checks the primitive3x3 estimated covariance before the redundant total target is appended.",
    "The exact runtime estimates target-specific and polarized variance fits separately and then builds cross-covariances by polarization."
  ],
  "interpretation": "The true Gaussian primitive covariance is positive definite in all four cells. Scaling and correlation conditioning describe design sensitivity; they do not prove the mechanism of any estimated-variance failure. Separate fitted variance surfaces and finite simulated trace subtraction can yield an indefinite estimate even when the true covariance is positive definite. Recorded failure labels establish the gate encountered but do not identify which primitive/polarized smoother failed first."
}
